{"id": "EUVD-2026-86899", "enisaUuid": "00143873-7041-3928-8e87-060ee323a694", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ns390/crypto: Fix handling of EBUSY in PHMAC when req is pushed to crypto engine\n\nWhen a request is transferred to the engine via\ncrypto_transfer_hash_request_to_engine() there are two return codes\nsignaling a successful transfer: EINPROGRESS and EBUSY. However the\ncorrect handling of EBUSY was missing and has been added as a return\ncode indicating a successful transfer to the crypto engine.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:08", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:09:55", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/203702f0013f9b7324e8c5facb6cd6e9c0942b13", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bcd7f1f1e2f2882ad206f72425255be105178151", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/330148371401de474b656eaf521861f12ec1a1ce"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97591", "GHSA-48x9-wv7p-5368"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a0a13b7-99f2-32ee-8f3c-786a98360e8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "1c382621-ce46-36a4-a89b-10dc89269ef6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cbbc675506cc4cd93e6f895e7c1f693156f9a95c <203702f0013f9b7324e8c5facb6cd6e9c0942b13"}, {"id": "27226d24-2596-3313-ace8-470549c95dbb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "48a51528-9950-353d-a116-25631b625508", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "b6ec4dd5-7a12-3ac3-8261-1988b3b78668", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "c787156c-2921-385d-a709-d2b2b9ff0b76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ce843122-79f8-3273-a8bc-2c3ea36fefe1", "product": {"name": "Linux",